  <h1>About Korea Explained</h1>
  <p>
    Korea Explained is a small network of guides written for English-speaking readers curious
    about Korea — its culture, food, entertainment, and everyday life. It's organized into
    four sections:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/korea/">Korea, Explained</a> — culture, travel, and everyday life</li>
    <li><a href="/recipes/">Korean Recipes, Explained</a> — approachable home cooking</li>
    <li><a href="/entertainment/">K-Entertainment, Explained</a> — context for K-pop, K-dramas, and film</li>
    <li><a href="/beauty/">K-Beauty, Explained</a> — Korean skincare, explained plainly</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Posts start as AI-assisted drafts and are reviewed and edited by a human before publishing,
    with the goal of adding original, practical detail rather than just summarizing what's
    already online.
  </p>
  <p>
    This site is written and edited by Chris Kim, who reviews, fact-checks, and
    edits every post before it's published.
  </p>
  <p>
    Have a topic suggestion or a correction? Reach out via the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
  </p>
